; ONE BLOCK FOLDED INTO A GHASH  which is Y = (Y xor X) dot H;
;
; NIST SP 800_38D section 6 point 4; aes/gcm128 does this three times: over
; the associated data  over the ciphertext  and over the length block; The
; three are the same seven hundred lines  so they are one file;
;
; Entered and left at the caller's own nought; the block to fold is at
; @0x3db:0x3ea and is SPENT  the accumulator at @0x3eb:0x3fa is replaced  and
; the subkey at @0x3a5:0x3b4 is COPIED and survives;
;
; THE SUBKEY SURVIVES AND THE BLOCK DOES NOT  and that asymmetry is the whole
; of the bookkeeping here; block/ghashmul spends both of ITS operands  so the
; accumulator MOVES into the bit source and the subkey is COPIED into the
; value; A GCM folds as many blocks as the message has and every one of them
; wants H again;
;
; THE BLOCK IS LEFT CLEAR  which is what lets the caller build the next one by
; sliding bytes into it without clearing first; the exclusive or consumes it
; a byte at a time on a conveyor;
;
; CONTRACTS ARE RELATIVE; this block is included at offset nought three times
; so they resolve to the addresses aes/gcm128's tape map names;
;
; ASSERT ptr=+0

